of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">On each public photo press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b>. The editor opens.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The box over the plate is already suggested: as soon as the review opens, every outside photo (the More outside photos included) gets its suggestion, and those photos show Box suggested. Check it. <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-out and check-in photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner, documents, tracker</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line', 'chapter', 'live-visitors-and-live-chat', 'Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.

## The inbox

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.
2. Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo''s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.
3. Write a text and press **Send text**: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. **Suggest a reply** puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.
4. Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.
5. **Stop texts** stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. **Match automatically again** undoes a link made by hand.

## Missed calls

A missed call raises the task "Missed call from ..." for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.

> Tip: Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, "Missed call: text the caller back"), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo''s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.

## Calls and texts on records

A booking''s History tab, a renter''s page and an owner''s page have "Calls and texts": the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries with that person. Calls are not recorded on the line for now, so there is no transcript or recording to show.

## Quo contacts

Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.

- A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.
- One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.
- A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.
- If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.
- **Settings**, **Quo contacts**: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and **Sync everyone again**. Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)", turn it off.

## Booking texts

Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and **Settings**, **Text alerts**).

## The settings

Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)": the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Today** > **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls**; press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. To use the phone''s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** in **Settings** > **Program**. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.', 'Texts and calls (the Quo phone line)', 'Texts and calls in the chat inbox, unknown callers, missed calls, booking texts, call summaries and the settings.',
  'Every call and text on the CarmaCars number (Quo) is kept and matched to the person: staff, a renter and their booking, an owner or a lead. Staff answer texts from the same inbox as live chat. It is on by default; Program settings switch each part.

## The inbox

1. Open **Today** > **Visitors**, the **Chat** tab, and press **Texts and calls**. Each number shows who it is (Renter, Owner, Lead, Staff or Unknown caller), unread texts and missed calls.
2. Choose a number. Calls and texts are in order; a call shows its length, and Quo''s summary or a one-line AI summary when there is one.
3. Write a text and press **Send text**: it goes from the CarmaCars number through Quo. **Suggest a reply** puts an AI draft in the box; nothing is ever sent until you press Send text.
4. Beside the conversation: the renter with their bookings, the owner or the lead. A caller who gave the same phone in live chat or a discount game shows their visit on the site.
5. **Stop texts** stops every text to the number, booking texts included. A person who texts STOP is stopped the same way; START allows texts again.

## Unknown callers

Press **Unknown callers**. For a number nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press **Create lead**, or find the renter and press **Link to** the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. **Match automatically again** undoes a link made by hand.

## Missed calls

A missed call raises the task "Missed call from ..." for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.

> Tip: Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, "Missed call: text the caller back"), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo''s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.

## Calls and texts on records

A booking''s History tab, a renter''s page and an owner''s page have "Calls and texts": the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries with that person. Calls are not recorded on the line for now, so there is no transcript or recording to show.

## Quo contacts

Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.

- A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site''s version is sent again.
- One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.
- A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.
- If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.
- **Settings**, **Quo contacts**: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and **Sync everyone again**. Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)", turn it off.

## Booking texts

Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and **Settings**, **Text alerts**).

## The settings

Program settings, "Phone and texts (Quo)": the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).


## Call and Text buttons

Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map''s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.

1. Press **Text**: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press **Send**. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person''s conversation under **Today** > **Visitors** > **Chat** > **Texts and calls**; press **Open the conversation** to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.
2. Press **Call**: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo''s desktop app is your computer''s calling app, tick **On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app** once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.
3. Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.
4. To use the phone''s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** in **Settings** > **Program**. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone''s own apps too.

## The CarmaCars app links

**Settings** > **Program**, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see **Download the CarmaCars app** in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.
