&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>; press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-