- What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts, leads and hot visitors (customer service and Sales also get the last two).
- Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.
- Your own: **Alerts** > **Settings**.
- On or off for everyone: **Settings**, **Text alerts**, "Phone alerts".
- Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and **Alerts** > **Settings** says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.

## Lead and visitor alerts

Staff get an alert, in the app and on their phone, for what needs a person quickly. They are never emailed or texted, so the daily email limit is untouched. The Admins always get them (every device that turned alerts on, so both of you on the shared Admin account); the rest go to the person it concerns.

| What | Who gets it | Topic |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A new renter lead: the contact form, the phone number box, a discount game claim, the live chat. It names the source. | You, and the person the lead is assigned to; if nobody, customer service and Sales on duty | Leads |
| A request typed into the booking request or contact form and not sent (after the capture delay, 30 minutes) | The same | Leads |
| A new owner lead, including "Website form, unfinished", and again when an unfinished application becomes the 30-minute chase | You, and the Sales person it is assigned to | Leads |
| A visitor turns Hot on Live visitors (analytics consent only, once per visitor per day) | You, and customer service and Sales on duty | Visitors |

1. On duty means someone who had Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes.
2. A lead alert goes at once, at any hour, unless the person turned the **Leads** topic off on that device (**Alerts** > **Settings**).
3. More than 5 lead alerts in 10 minutes become one "N new leads" alert for the rest of that window.
4. Test and verification accounts never get them, and a test address never makes one.
5. The switches are under **Settings** > **Text alerts**, "Staff alerts for leads and visitors", all on. Live visitors'' own "notify hot" switch must also be on for the hot visitor alert.

> Watch out: customer service and Sales are only alerted while on duty. With nobody on duty, only the Admins are alerted; the lead is on Leads for the team in the morning.

## Everything else that alerts you

Every staff alert is one rule: what happens, who gets it and a tier. Urgent: on the phone at once, at any hour. Normal: on the phone, held until the quiet hours end. Digest: a line in **Alerts** only. All are on. What each one is and who gets it: the chapter "Alerts: the bell and your phone".

1. Switch a kind off or change its tier: **Alerts** (the bell) > **Settings**, "Which alerts staff get".
2. The amounts and timings (a payment over $500, passing on an unopened urgent alert after 15 minutes, the briefs, grouping, complaint words): **Settings** > **Text alerts**, "Staff alerts".
3. The App Store and Google Play links are empty until the app is published. When set, phones are asked to download the app instead of turning on browser alerts.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Every renter, owner, investor, staff member chooses how we reach them: Email, Text or Both. Texts go only to a phone they verified with a code, from the CarmaCars number, and each has a link to the page. It is on by default; nothing needs setting up.</p><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-who-gets-what" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who gets what</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Email</b>: emails only. <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a short text instead of the email. <b class="gd-ui">Both</b>: a text and the email.</li><li>Not chosen yet: Both for someone with a verified phone and an email, Text for an account made by phone without an email, otherwise Email.</li><li>No verified phone, a number that replied STOP, a US number while US texting waits for A2P 10DLC, or a number outside Canada and the US: email only.</li><li>Signed agreements, statements, receipts, invoices and notices are always emailed when there is an email address. Someone on Text also gets a text with a link to view or download it in their portal.</li><li>Every customer email has its own short text: renters, owners, investors, additional drivers, co-signers and leads. Only the sign-in and security emails (password reset, sign-in link, security notice, &quot;Continue your request&quot;) are never texts. A review request or a come-back offer is texted only when its email may go (marketing consent).</li><li>An additional driver&#39;s or a co-signer&#39;s link is texted to that person (their own account with a verified phone), never to the renter or owner.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-a-person-s-channel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A person&#39;s channel</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the renter, owner or investor under People. The card <b class="gd-ui">How we reach them</b> shows what they chose, what is used now and why, their verified phone, texts in the last 30 days and any STOP or START. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to set it (recorded in the audit log). Customer service and Sales can change a renter&#39;s or owner&#39;s; an investor&#39;s only Admins.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-stop-start-and-quiet-hours" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">STOP, START and quiet hours</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A reply STOP (or OPT OUT, UNSUBSCRIBE, CANCEL, END, QUIT) stops texts to the number at once; texts waiting are not sent and their emails go instead. START turns texts back on. Every STOP and START is logged.</li><li>Quo sends no confirmation, so we do: one text right away (quiet hours do not apply), &quot;CarmaCars: you&#39;re unsubscribed and won&#39;t get more texts. Reply START to resubscribe.&quot; after STOP, and &quot;CarmaCars: texts are back on. Reply STOP to opt out.&quot; after START. Once per change; the card How we reach them shows it as confirmed by text. A STOP or START you set by hand, or a carrier block, sends nothing.</li><li>The first automated text to a number, and the first after START, ends &quot;Reply STOP to opt out.&quot;</li><li>Quiet hours, 9 pm to 8 am Toronto time: texts that are not urgent wait and go at 8 am. Urgent: late return notices, pickup and return details on the day, breakdown, accident and a disabled car.</li><li>A text that is not sent after all (STOP, Quo refuses it, the person chose email meanwhile) sends the email it replaced.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-the-settings-and-the-texts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The settings and the texts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>: on or off, the defaults, the quiet hours, the STOP line, US numbers, and the text of each notification with a preview (edit, switch off, mark urgent). A text names CarmaCars, keeps {{link}}, has no long dash and is at most 320 characters; 160 is one text. The two confirmation texts (after STOP and START) are in the same settings. The generic text built from the email&#39;s subject is only for an email added later without its own text.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-booking-start-and-end" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking start and end</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking gets these by itself, by email, text and phone alert (each person&#39;s channel), once each, and again only when the time changes (an extension, a new pickup time):</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">When</th><th scope="col">The renter gets</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The day before pickup</td><td>What to bring, where and when</td></tr><tr><td>About 2 hours before pickup</td><td>&quot;See you at 2:00 pm today&quot;, the place and what to bring</td></tr><tr><td>30 minutes after a pickup nobody recorded</td><td>&quot;You&#39;re all set&quot;, the return time and place</td></tr><tr><td>The day before the return</td><td>The return time and place, fuel and keys</td></tr><tr><td>About 3 hours before the return</td><td>&quot;Your rental ends at 5:00 pm&quot;, fuel, clean, all keys and the offer &quot;Extend at 5% off: from $X for 1 more day&quot; with its link</td></tr><tr><td>At the return time</td><td>&quot;Your booking ended at 5:00 pm&quot;, return now, or the extend offer</td></tr><tr><td>15 minutes late</td><td>T13, the late notice</td></tr><tr><td>2 hours late</td><td>T14, the final notice</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A booking whose pickup nobody recorded counts as out: it gets the end messages, the late notices and the late tasks like a rental on rent. Its status stays as it is.</li><li>The late notices and the short reminders go from 7 am to 10 pm. Overnight they wait until 7 am; a car returned in the night gets nothing.</li><li>The late panel&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Send T13</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Send T14</b> send the same notices: never twice.</li><li>An insurer-billed booking messages the renter too: they hold the car.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded</b>: 30 minutes after the pickup time with nothing recorded, Fleet gets the task &quot;Record pickup for CC-xxxxx, or mark no-show&quot; and the field staff of the handover an alert and a text. At 3 hours the Admins get an alert and a task. They close by themselves once the pickup is recorded or the booking is cancelled.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Not back</b>: 15 minutes after the return time with no return recorded, the field staff of the return and the Admins get an alert and a text with the renter&#39;s name and phone, at any hour.</li><li>Each moment has its switch, all on: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Booking start and end&quot;. The text of each is in the list of texts on the same page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-texts-a-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts a day</h2><p class="gd-p">Site health on <b class="gd-ui">To do</b> has <b class="gd-ui">Texts today</b>: sent, notifications among them, failed, not sent and sign-in codes for the last 7 days, and the texts waiting for 8 am.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-phone-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Phone alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter, owner, investor and staff member can also get alerts on their phone or computer (web push), as well as their emails and texts. Each turns them on per device on their profile; the first page of each portal offers it once. On iPhone and iPad it works from the Home Screen app (Safari, <b class="gd-ui">Share</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add to Home Screen</b>; iOS 16.4 or later).</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What alerts: new requests and offers, booking changes, payments, pickups and returns (field jobs), messages, urgent alerts and documents to sign. Each person changes them; the defaults: renters everything, owners new bookings, changes, payments, incidents and documents, staff requests, changes, messages and urgent alerts, field staff their jobs and pay, Admins requests, payments, messages and urgent alerts, leads and hot visitors (customer service and Sales also get the last two).</li><li>Sign-in links and codes, digests and marketing never come as alerts. An alert that is not urgent waits for the quiet hours to end for customers; an alert already read in the portal is not sent.</li><li>Your own: <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>.</li><li>On or off for everyone: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Phone alerts&quot;.</li><li>Setup: nothing to do. The deploy makes the two keys alerts need once and keeps them; until the first deploy after this release the cards are hidden and <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> says so. A phone that uninstalled the app or turned alerts off is removed by itself.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-lead-and-visitor-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead and visitor alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff get an alert, in the app and on their phone, for what needs a person quickly. They are never emailed or texted, so the daily email limit is untouched. The Admins always get them (every device that turned alerts on, so both of you on the shared Admin account); the rest go to the person it concerns.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Who gets it</th><th scope="col">Topic</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A new renter lead: the contact form, the phone number box, a discount game claim, the live chat. It names the source.</td><td>You, and the person the lead is assigned to; if nobody, customer service and Sales on duty</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A request typed into the booking request or contact form and not sent (after the capture delay, 30 minutes)</td><td>The same</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A new owner lead, including &quot;Website form, unfinished&quot;, and again when an unfinished application becomes the 30-minute chase</td><td>You, and the Sales person it is assigned to</td><td>Leads</td></tr><tr><td>A visitor turns Hot on Live visitors (analytics consent only, once per visitor per day)</td><td>You, and customer service and Sales on duty</td><td>Visitors</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On duty means someone who had Live chat, Live visitors or Texts open in the last 15 minutes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A lead alert goes at once, at any hour, unless the person turned the <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> topic off on that device (<b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">More than 5 lead alerts in 10 minutes become one &quot;N new leads&quot; alert for the rest of that window.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Test and verification accounts never get them, and a test address never makes one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The switches are under <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Staff alerts for leads and visitors&quot;, all on. Live visitors&#39; own &quot;notify hot&quot; switch must also be on for the hot visitor alert.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>customer service and Sales are only alerted while on duty. With nobody on duty, only the Admins are alerted; the lead is on Leads for the team in the morning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="text-alerts-email-text-or-both-everything-else-that-alerts-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Everything else that alerts you</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff alert is one rule: what happens, who gets it and a tier. Urgent: on the phone at once, at any hour. Normal: on the phone, held until the quiet hours end. Digest: a line in <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> only. All are on. What each one is and who gets it: the chapter &quot;Alerts: the bell and your phone&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Switch a kind off or change its tier: <b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b> (the bell) &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, &quot;Which alerts staff get&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The amounts and timings (a payment over $500, passing on an unopened urgent alert after 15 minutes, the briefs, grouping, complaint words): <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>, &quot;Staff alerts&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The App Store and Google Play links are empty until the app is published. When set, phones are asked to download the app instead of turning on browser alerts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'advertising-and-owner-recruitment', 'chapter', 'academy', 'Marketing writes the text of every ad from the car''s own record, keeps track of where each ad is posted, tells the sales assistants when an ad needs updating, shows which channels bring bookings, drafts the week''s Facebook Page and Instagram posts and keeps the consent log for owner recruitment. Nothing is posted by the server: you post by hand, and Facebook Marketplace from the owner''s own profile, with a kit and a daily rotation under Marketplace.

## Facebook Marketplace

**Marketing** > **Marketplace**. Listings go up from the owner''s own Facebook profile (business Pages cannot post vehicles), by Claude in the owner''s Chrome or by a person. The playbook is docs/runbooks/marketplace.md.

1. **Today** lists what is due: **Update the price** and **Take down** first, then up to the day''s allowance of new posts and renewals (4 a day by default: 3 to 5 a day avoids spam flags). **Coming up** shows the next days.
2. Press **Kit** on a car. The kit shows every field of facebook.com/marketplace/create/vehicle in the form''s order (location, year, make, model, mileage, price, body style, colours, condition, fuel, transmission), each with **Copy**, the description in Marketplace style, and the tracked link.
3. Press **Download the photos (ZIP)**. It has the 10 best photos named 01 to 10. Add them in that order: the first is the cover.
4. Post it. Then press **Posted** on Today and paste the listing''s address. Press **Renewed**, **Updated** or **Taken down** the same way when you do those.
5. **Inbox replies for this car** has the answers for price, availability, requirements, deposit, delivery and "send your number", filled in for the car. Each one ends with the car''s link or asks for a phone number.
6. After answering the inbox, open **Log an inbox session**. Enter the number of chats and the numbers collected, one per line (name, phone, car code). Each new number becomes a lead, and customer service gets a call-back task due within 15 minutes.

- Kits are made when the page opens, so their prices are today''s. A price change marks the live listing **Update the price** and opens the usual update task.
- A car that does not take requests, has no daily rate or has only sample photos says **Do not post yet**.
- **Rotation settings** change the posts a day, the days before a renewal, and the default location (a car''s home area wins).
- The booking request asks "How did you hear about us?" (optional). Bookings by channel counts the answer after staff''s source and a tracked visit.

## Write an ad

**Marketing** > **Ads**, the **Ad listings** tab.

1. Choose the car and the channel (Facebook Marketplace, Kijiji, Craigslist, Instagram, Facebook Page or Google Business Profile) and press **Write it**.
2. Copy each part with its button: the title, the price line, the description (or caption), the hashtags and the tracked link. Each shows its length against the channel''s limit (a Kijiji title takes 64 characters, Craigslist 70, an Instagram caption 2,200, a Google post 1,500).
3. Add the photos in the order shown: the first is the cover. Open a photo to save it.
4. Post the ad on the site, then press **Mark as posted** and paste its address and the date.

- The text comes from the car''s record only: the rates, kilometres, deposit, delivery fee, who may rent it and the car code. A fact the record does not have is left out. No review, rating or claim is added.
- The tracked link opens the car''s page with utm_source (the channel), utm_medium and utm_campaign (the car code), so the request counts under that channel.
- A warning shows when the car does not take requests, has no daily rate, or shows sample photos (take real photos first: an ad shows the car itself).
- Facebook Marketplace is posted from the owner''s own Facebook profile in their browser: Meta does not take vehicle listings from business Pages. Kijiji takes one ad per car, in one category and one region. An Instagram caption cannot hold a working link: put it in the bio or a story link sticker.

## When an ad needs updating

**Marketing** > **Posted ads**, or the task in **Today** > **Staff tasks**.

1. A change of 3% or more in a car''s daily, weekend, weekly or 30-day rate, any change of its deposit, kilometres, extra-km price or delivery fee, or the car leaving the site marks each of its live ads Needs updating and opens a task for the sales assistants (for example Update the Kijiji ad and the car). The task says what changed, the new price line and the ad''s address.
2. Press **New text**, copy the new text and update the ad on the site.
3. Press **Mark the ad updated**. The task closes. Closing the task in Staff tasks counts too.
4. Car off the site: take the ad down and press **Taken down**. If the car comes back at the same rates first, the task is cancelled by itself.

> Good to know: The 3% is under **Settings** > **Program**, Advertising and owner recruitment. The rates are checked again every 6 hours, so a rate dated ahead is caught on its day.

## Bookings by channel

**Marketing** > **Bookings by channel**.

- Every request of the dates chosen counts once: under the source staff set on the booking, else the renter''s visit (the campaign source of a tracked link, or the site they came from), else a referral code, else how it reached us (phone, email, WhatsApp).
- Choose the last visit before the request or the first visit. A booking is a request that was confirmed, paid or completed; revenue is its rental charge after discounts. The months add up to the Bookings list.
- The visit is kept with the request when it is sent, so the source outlives the 90 days of visit history. A visitor who refused analytics cookies has no source.
- On a booking, the line Came from shows the source. Press **Set** to give it by hand when the renter told you (a Kijiji reply, a walk-in, word of mouth).

## Facebook Page and Instagram drafts

**Marketing** > **Social drafts**.

1. The week''s drafts are written from the fleet every 6 hours, for this week and the next: Monday a new car (published in the last 14 days) or a featured one; Tuesday the owner program; Thursday the cars free this weekend; Friday the requirements (Instagram); Sunday a price highlight or a seasonal trip (Facebook Page). Press **Write drafts for this week** to write them now.
2. Read each draft. Press **Edit** to change the caption, the channels or the day, then **Approve**; or press **Skip**.
3. Copy the caption for each channel (on the Facebook Page the tracked link is in the text; for Instagram copy the link for the bio), post it with the photos shown, then press **Posted on Instagram** or **Posted on Facebook Page** and paste the post''s address.

- Wednesday''s walkaround video and Saturday''s handover story are filmed by field staff. No renter is shown without written consent.
- Press **Add a post of your own** at the bottom of the week for anything else.

## Meta publishing (off until set up)

**Settings** > **Meta publishing**. Until it is on, every post is copied and posted by hand.

1. Make the Instagram account a professional account and link it to the CarmaCars Facebook Page.
2. At developers.facebook.com, create a Business app owned by the CarmaCars business portfolio. Give it the permissions pages_show_list, pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic and instagram_content_publish, and make a long-lived Page access token. Meta may ask for App Review before posts are public.
3. Press **Enter the details**: the Page id, the Instagram account id and the token. The token goes to the vault; the page shows only its last four characters.
4. Press **Switch on**. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press **Switch off** or **Remove the token** at any time.

## Owner recruitment

**Marketing** > **Owner recruitment**.

Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.

1. Press **Add a lead**: paste the ad''s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.
2. Call them with the script on the lead''s page and press **Log the call**. A yes needs their words ("Yes, text me the details"): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.
3. When the lead''s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press **Send**. The email adds CarmaCars'' name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with "Reply STOP to opt out." Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.

- Press **Record consent** for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no "no solicitation" note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).
- The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.
- A message without consent is refused with the reason. **Settings** > **Program** has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.

> Watch out: Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.


## Owner pipeline

Open **Marketing** > **Owner pipeline**. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of eight columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner''s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and **Add an owner lead**. A visitor who starts the application is a lead as soon as a valid email or mobile is typed (Website form, unfinished), with the car they entered or priced in the earnings calculator; the same email or phone joins the lead already open.

1. Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.
2. They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.
3. They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press **They replied**), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. **Stop follow-ups** and **Restart follow-ups** are on each card.
4. **Move** changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner''s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.
5. Customer service sees the same board in the staff portal. Sales see only the owners they invited, added or were given, on My sales.
6. A new website lead goes to the least busy Sales person, never to a verification or test account (with no real Sales person on, it waits unassigned). Test accounts are never "sourced by" on a real lead or owner, nor given its task.
7. An application left unfinished for 30 minutes goes to the least busy Sales person with a task, and its follow-ups say "finish your application" with a link that opens their saved answers. When they send it, the card moves to Applied and the follow-ups stop.
8. Leads that came in before the automatic follow-ups existed and that nobody moved are in To do as a task "Follow up now" with their name: call or email them, then move the card.

### Owner referral links

An owner''s link for new owners is `carmacars.ca/r/<their code>?to=owner` (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner''s car. It shows under **Owner referral credits** as due; pay it with the owner''s payout and press **Mark paid**.

## Listing channels

Open **Marketing** > **Listing channels**: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).

1. Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press **Update** to change them, **Add a channel** for a new one.
2. None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel''s address: **JSON**, **CSV** or **XML** (the XML is in the shape of Google''s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.
3. Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner''s car (01 Motors or any other). **Keep out** takes a car out of every feed.
4. **New key** ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.
