acters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch on</b>. Approved drafts then go out on their day and their post links are recorded; a refusal shows on the draft. Press <b class="gd-ui">Switch off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove the token</b> at any time.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-recruitment" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner recruitment</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner recruitment</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">Owners and co-hosts are found in classified ads. The anti-spam law (CASL) does not cover a live phone call, but an email or a text needs consent, names the sender and offers an unsubscribe. The lawyer confirms the approach before outreach starts.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a lead</b>: paste the ad&#39;s address, choose who is selling (a private seller, a dealer or a rental business) and type the name, the phone and the car from the ad. Nothing is collected from the classified site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Call them with the script on the lead&#39;s page and press <b class="gd-ui">Log the call</b>. A yes needs their words (&quot;Yes, text me the details&quot;): they become express consent in the log. A no means do not contact, ever.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the lead&#39;s page says email or text is allowed, choose a template, check the words and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. The email adds CarmaCars&#39; name, mailing address and the unsubscribe link; the text ends with &quot;Reply STOP to opt out.&quot; Texts wait for 8 am during quiet hours.</div></li></ol></div><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Press <b class="gd-ui">Record consent</b> for consent given another way: express (with its proof), implied by their inquiry (6 months), implied by a business relationship (2 years), a business address published with no &quot;no solicitation&quot; note (never a private seller), or one message after a referral (naming the referrer).</li><li>The consent log is never edited: a change is a new line. An unsubscribe or a STOP reply adds a withdrawal by itself, and nothing more goes on that channel.</li><li>A message without consent is refused with the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> has a switch that stops all recruitment messages.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Keep the proof of an oral yes: a recording, or a note written during the call with the time. Consent you cannot show does not count.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-owner-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner pipeline</b>. Every prospective owner is one card, in one of eight columns: New, Contacted, Call booked, Applied, Agreement sent, Signed, Car onboarded and Lost. Leads come from the owner form on the website, an owner&#39;s referral link, Owner recruitment (classified ads) and <b class="gd-ui">Add an owner lead</b>. A visitor who starts the application is a lead as soon as a valid email or mobile is typed (Website form, unfinished), with the car they entered or priced in the earnings calculator; the same email or phone joins the lead already open.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-up emails go by themselves on day 0, 2, 5 and 10 after a lead comes in: the owner program in plain words (the car goes on our fleet insurance policy, we rent it out in Toronto and pay the owner every month; fees apply) and the link to apply. They are marketing emails: they wait behind every other email under the daily limit, go in the sending hours and carry the unsubscribe link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They go only with consent: a website inquiry counts for 6 months, a classified-ad lead needs consent in its log, and a referral typed by staff gets one message only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">They stop when the lead replies (a text or a call from their number, or press <b class="gd-ui">They replied</b>), when the stage changes, when they unsubscribe, and after the last one. <b class="gd-ui">Stop follow-ups</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Restart follow-ups</b> are on each card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Move</b> changes the stage (with a note, and why when lost). Agreement sent, Signed and Car onboarded also follow the owner&#39;s records: an owner agreement sent or signed, a car on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Customer service sees the same board in the staff portal. Sales see only the owners they invited, added or were given, on My sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new website lead goes to the least busy Sales person, never to a verification or test account (with no real Sales person on, it waits unassigned). Test accounts are never &quot;sourced by&quot; on a real lead or owner, nor given its task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">An application left unfinished for 30 minutes goes to the least busy Sales person with a task, and its follow-ups say &quot;finish your application&quot; with a link that opens their saved answers. When they send it, the card moves to Applied and the follow-ups stop.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Leads that came in before the automatic follow-ups existed and that nobody moved are in To do as a task &quot;Follow up now&quot; with their name: call or email them, then move the card.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Owner referral links</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner&#39;s link for new owners is <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/r/&lt;their code&gt;?to=owner</span> (the list is at the bottom of the board). A new owner who applies after it is credited to that owner. The credit follows the referral kickback rule: the Kickback Rate (20%) of the Rental Charge of the first completed rental of the new owner&#39;s car. It shows under <b class="gd-ui">Owner referral credits</b> as due; pay it with the owner&#39;s payout and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark paid</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="advertising-and-owner-recruitment-listing-channels" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listing channels</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listing channels</b>: the sites and directories where our cars can be listed beyond carmacars.ca (Turo, Getaround, Google Business Profile, Google Merchant Center, the Meta catalog, Kijiji, Facebook Marketplace, KAYAK, Expedia, Discover Cars, Rentalcars.com, Craigslist, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, YellowPages and any you add).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each has a status (Not started, Applied, Live, Paused, Not for us), who holds the login, notes and how listing works there. Press <b class="gd-ui">Update</b> to change them, <b class="gd-ui">Add a channel</b> for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">None is connected by itself: apply on the site. When a site or partner program takes a feed, give it that channel&#39;s address: <b class="gd-ui">JSON</b>, <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> or <b class="gd-ui">XML</b> (the XML is in the shape of Google&#39;s vehicle listings feed). Car links carry the channel, so its bookings show in Bookings by channel.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every feed has our own and co-hosted cars on the site, never a partner&#39;s car (01 Motors or any other). <b class="gd-ui">Keep out</b> takes a car out of every feed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old address. Each feed is read at most 60 times an hour and each answer is kept 15 minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'chapter', 'advertising-and-owner-recruitment', 'The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site''s own checks and published by themselves (the website''s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.

## The copy of a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.

1. The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car''s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.
2. Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what''s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.
3. To change a field press **Change**, then **Save and lock**. A locked field is kept by every new version. **Unlock** lets it be written again.
4. **Write again** asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car''s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.

> Good to know: The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car''s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.

## Landing pages and guides

**Settings**, then Search.

1. Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).
2. Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.
3. Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. A page for a way of renting (monthly, SUV) goes into search once enough real cars match it (Program settings).
4. Open **Edit** on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. **Write again** asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.

## Vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...

1. Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.
2. One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: **Index the place pages**, **Index the colour pages**, **Index the search term pages**, **Index the /buy pages**, **Index the detailing pages**, **Index the body shop pages**. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.
3. The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.
4. **Financing disclaimer**: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.
5. Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (Pro, 6,144 MB, by default; Free, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.
6. Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.
7. Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People > Renters, the Leads tab.
8. Settings: **Index every page** (the default) or **Only pages that pass the rules**: makes, models with 2 or more years of data, years with one of our cars or of a popular model from 2015, trims with one of our cars. The others stay visible but out of search. Also the gas, premium and electricity prices, and how often the catalog is imported (every 30 days).
9. Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. **Add trims for another model** adds a model that has none.
10. Catalog import: the last import and its counts. **Import now** asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.

> Good to know: A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car''s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.

## Stock photos on the vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: "Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons". The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.

1. Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet''s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked "not the exact year"; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.
2. The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.
3. Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press **Hide**. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.
4. **Pick again** asks for the next best photo; **Replace** takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.
5. **Show stock photos** in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).

> Good to know: Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer''s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.

## A car for sale

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car. On the For sale card, tick **For sale**, enter the Asking price and press **Save**.

1. The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.
2. Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.
3. "Find me this car" on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: **Owner leads**, Buyer leads), with a To do line.

## Search engines and business listings

**Settings**, then Site settings.

1. Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.
2. Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.
3. Business listings: press **Copy** beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.

> Good to know: Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.

## Place pages

Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. **Settings**, then Search.

1. Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.
2. Quality gate: off. On, only places within the delivery reach are in search, and rental pages only with a real matching car. Search engines can treat many similar pages as low value; the gate lowers that risk.
3. Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.
4. Regions and places: every province, state and territory is on. Untick a region to take its pages and sitemaps off the site.
5. Terms and services: change a term''s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term (its pages then leave search), switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for "price on request".

> Good to know: A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.

## Requests from the place pages

The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in **To do**: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages say plainly that CarmaCars does not sell, finance or lease cars; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.

Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as "Auto services we arrange": a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. CarmaCars does not do this work, and the pages say so: each takes a request (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.

## One name, address and phone

The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.

## What search engines may read

**Settings**, **Vehicle pages**, **Search scope** says what search engines are invited to read:

- **Full (every page)**, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website''s CPU time as crawlers read them.
- **Core (about 23,000 pages)**: the fixed pages, the fleet''s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.

The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month''s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all ("try again tomorrow") until the month resets. People always get every page.

## IndexNow

**Search**, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own; a refusal waits an hour, then longer. Sweep: the priority list once a week; a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row.
